            {
                "entry_id": "9822ed40-e745-3bc1-ac6a-9574a72349d4",
                "word": "indigenist",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "57c85d67-b21f-46dd-b5c3-9dbe5a655d40",
                        "entry_id": "9822ed40-e745-3bc1-ac6a-9574a72349d4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "indigenists"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d30d9224-c962-33aa-a805-4e83ac530bf8",
                        "entry_id": "9822ed40-e745-3bc1-ac6a-9574a72349d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who supports indigenous people or beliefs."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a53f5779-9cf2-45dd-9851-c217dca4a592",
                                "sense_id": "d30d9224-c962-33aa-a805-4e83ac530bf8",
                                "text": "Thus, the political skills displayed by the Yshiro leaders, even when seen by radical indigenists as stemming from hunting—gathering skills, appeared as a possible index of inauthenticity to the extent that they seem to alter the egalitarianism of hunter-gatherer societies."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c91b5890-3905-4596-8ab4-4026579ef8cd",
                                "sense_id": "d30d9224-c962-33aa-a805-4e83ac530bf8",
                                "text": "However, even within the framework of political support for insurgent Indians, the Utopian dimension of the indigenists remained predominant—they spent much time discussing indigenous music, languages and crafts, but little mention was made of the distribution of land for which Indians were fighting to the death against the Leguía regime."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e044b162-ecbe-477e-bebe-052dfcb6434a",
                                "sense_id": "d30d9224-c962-33aa-a805-4e83ac530bf8",
                                "text": "For indigenists, benefits included a new and potentially more compelling frame in which to promote their advocacy of indigenous selfdetermination."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
